{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":27610,"name":"xjd","username":"xjd","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/xjd/{size}/3935_2.png","created_at":"2026-11-20T00:55:32.961Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003ePort c-kzg-4844 to CKB-VM; see \u003ca href=\"https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-4844\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eEIP-4844\u003c/a\u003e for more details.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe also introduce a \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/XuJiandong/c-kzg-4844/blob/port-riscv/blob-tree/tutorial/README.md\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eblob tree\u003c/a\u003e built on c-kzg-4844. We already have SMT, but SMT proofs are quite large, especially when proving multiple elements at once. So we propose a new solution: the blob tree. At its core, it is a two-level path tree built on c-kzg-4844 with Shplonk. It commits to as many as 16,777,216 (4096×4096) elements in a tree of just two levels. Whether you query one element or many, the proof reduces to a single KZG verification call.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"onebox githubfolder\" data-onebox-src=\"https://github.com/XuJiandong/c-kzg-4844/tree/port-riscv\"\u003e\n  \u003cheader class=\"source\"\u003e\n      \u003cimg src=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/original/2X/b/bad3e5f9ad67c1ddf145107ce7032ac1d7b22563.svg\" class=\"site-icon\" alt=\"\" data-dominant-color=\"\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\"\u003e\n\n      \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/XuJiandong/c-kzg-4844/tree/port-riscv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003egithub.com\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/header\u003e\n\n  \u003carticle class=\"onebox-body\"\u003e\n    \u003ch3\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/XuJiandong/c-kzg-4844/tree/port-riscv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eGitHub - XuJiandong/c-kzg-4844: A minimal implementation of the Polynomial...\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n  \u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/XuJiandong/c-kzg-4844/tree/port-riscv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener no